<title>UK: Severn leads sector lower on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Severn leads sector lower on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Severn Trent Water Plc led the UK water sector lower on Tuesday as investors took profits after the recent rally and switched into shares that have underperformed, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1319 GMT, Severn Trent shares were off 13p to 871.</p>
<p>Shares in Anglian Group Plc eased 7-1/2p to 797-1/2, while shares in South West Water Plc fell 10p to 796-1/2. Shares in United Utilities Plc lost 8-1/2p to 723.</p>
</text>
